---
references:
  book:
    id: book
    title: A Book
  paper:
    id: paper
    title: A Paper
---

A `field.*` block moves a position (§6.1) and can rename a public field (D-4).
This entry puts `reference_id` in the tick and the author's own `locator` in the
bare content, while the node publishes them as `ref_id` and `loc` and numbers them
as `no`. `stable_fields = ["reference_id", "locator"]` is what keeps the pair
meaningful: the identity follows the **names**, never the positions:

Minim [^p. 1 `book`]@@citeShort esse.

Second [^"p. 2" `paper`]@@citeShort.

Assigning one slot position voids the whole preset (D-7), so a head that leaves
`reference_id` unassigned is an error rather than a citation — the bare content
stays the author's own field:

[^p. 9]@@citeShort

The same citation seen twice keeps one number, because `stable_fields` lists
`reference_id` and `locator` and both match:

[^p. 1 `book`]@@citeShort again.
